@host = https://localhost:7027

### 1) Without token: must return 401
GET {{host}}/api/objectives/mine

### 2) Login as employee
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "employee@test.com",
  "password": "Test@123"
}

### 3) With token: must return 200
GET {{host}}/api/objectives/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 4) Create an objective with token
POST {{host}}/api/objectives
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learn JWT",
  "description": "Understand how the token works",
  "startDate": "2026-11-16T00:00:00Z",
  "endDate": "2026-12-16T00:00:00Z"
}
### 5) Create + submit as employee
# @name create
POST {{host}}/api/objectives
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Needs approval",
  "description": "test",
  "startDate": "2026-11-16T00:00:00Z",
  "endDate": "2026-12-16T00:00:00Z"
}

###
POST {{host}}/api/objectives/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 6) Login as manager
# @name loginManager
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manager@test.com",
  "password": "Test@123"
}

### 7) Manager sees the pending list
GET {{host}}/api/objectives/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.$.token}}

### 8) Manager approves
POST {{host}}/api/objectives/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.$.token}}

### 9) Employee tries to approve: must be 403
POST {{host}}/api/objectives/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
### 11) Manager lists his team members
GET {{host}}/api/evaluations/team-members
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.$.token}}

### 12) Manager evaluates the employee (id 3)
POST {{host}}/api/evaluations
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 3,
  "period": "2026 Q4",
  "score": 85.5,
  "comment": "Good progress on objectives"
}

### 13) Employee sees his evaluations: must be 200 with one item
GET {{host}}/api/evaluations/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 14) Employee tries to create: must be 403
POST {{host}}/api/evaluations
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": 3, "period": "2026 Q4", "score": 90, "comment": "x" }

### 15) Manager evaluates himself: must be 400
POST {{host}}/api/evaluations
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": 2, "period": "2026 Q4", "score": 90, "comment": "x" }
### 16) Manager sees all objectives of his team: must be 200
GET {{host}}/api/objectives/team
Authorization: Bearer {{loginManager.response.body.$.token}}
